title: Diplomacy
subtitle: Talk to the Separatists before it is too late, or after.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_peace.svg
view-if: diplomacy_timer <= 0 and rc_in_govt and (dooku_movement or war) and not federal_compact
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; diplomacy_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "diplomacy"
new-page: true

= Diplomacy

The government can open official talks with the Separatist Parliament on Raxus. Our peace channels are [+ peace_talks +]/3 established. [? if bonteri_dead : With Mina Bonteri dead, the Separatist moderates have lost their bravest voice. ?]

- @talks: Open formal talks with the Separatist Parliament.
- @neutrals: Ask the Council of Neutral Systems to mediate.
- @compact: Propose a Federal Compact.
- @recognise: Recognise the Confederacy's independence.
- @easy_discard

@talks
view-if: peace_talks < 3
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Hawks and the Security Bloc object.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; peace_talks += 1; cis_relation += 6; sec_relation -= 5; hawk_dissent += 4

Envoys meet in a neutral system. The first session lasts eleven minutes. The second lasts eleven hours.

@neutrals
view-if: peace_talks < 3
subtitle: +1 peace channel; the Independents approve.
on-arrival: peace_talks += 1; ind_relation += 5; satine_mediation = 1

Duchess Satine of Mandalore agrees to host talks on behalf of the Council of Neutral Systems.

@compact
view-if: peace_talks >= 3
subtitle: −2 political capital. A reformed Republic in which the seceded worlds could live. Needs a Senate majority.
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 2; SW.federalCompact(Q); if (Q.federal_compact) this.achieve('federal_compact'); !}
go-to: fc_outcome

@fc_outcome

[+ vote_html +]

[? if federal_compact : The Senate approves the Federal Compact. Seceded worlds may return with guarantees of autonomy, fair representation and an end to guild monopolies. Within weeks, system after system lowers the Confederate flag. The guns fall silent. ?][? if fc_sabotaged : The Senate approves the Compact, but on the night it is to be signed, a bomb destroys the Separatist delegation's ship. Each side blames the other. The war resumes, more bitter than before. Someone did not want peace. ?][? if not fc_passed and not vote_tabled : The Compact fails on the floor. The Chancellor's allies call it "surrender with a ribbon on it". ?]

@recognise
view-if: war and (war_balance <= -2 or war_weariness >= 60)
subtitle: End the war by letting the Separatists go. The Republic would be smaller, and Palpatine would lose his war.
on-arrival: {!
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.35, guild: 0.55, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.05, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.0, cis: 1}, false);
st.mod += Q.war_weariness / 200; st.ind += Q.war_weariness / 200;
Q.rec_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'peace');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Treaty of Separation', Q.rec_vote);
if (Q.rec_vote >= 50) { Q.recognized_cis = 1; Q.war = 0; Q.dissolved = 1; Q.game_ending = 1; }
else { Q.hawk_dissent += 10; Q.faith -= 2; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if recognized_cis : The Senate votes to let the Confederacy go. The war is over. The Republic is smaller, poorer and humbled, but it is still a republic. ?][? if not recognized_cis : The Senate refuses. "We will not dismember the Republic," thunders [? if rc_chancellor : the Security Bloc's spokesman?][? if not rc_chancellor : the Chancellor's spokesman?]. ?]
